          "The engine rigorously enforces the mathematical ordering mandated by customs jurisprudence. Landing charges, historically computed at one percent of CIF value, are explicitly set to zero in compliance with CBIC Notification No. 91/2017-Customs and the Supreme Court decision in Commissioner of Customs v. Wipro Ltd. Basic Customs Duty is computed directly on the statutory Assessable Value (AV). Social Welfare Surcharge is calculated at exactly ten percent of the aggregate BCD liability, representing the statutory levy introduced by the Finance Act, 2018, in substitution of earlier education cesses. Integrated GST is then computed on the cumulative base comprising Assessable Value plus BCD plus SWS, exactly as required under Section 3(7) of the CTA. This multi-tiered cascading tax architecture ensures that indirect taxes reflect the true landed cost of imported commodities.",
